+```markdown
+# Baseten vs Aegis: Decision Matrix & Integration Guidance
+
+Summary:
+- Baseten: hosted, managed inference and model deployment platform — fast to use, low ops.
+- Aegis: full enterprise AI platform — heavy on governance, multi-domain integrations (HPC, QPU, Edge), billing/accounting, and compliance.
+
+Decision matrix (high-level):
+
+| Concern / Use case | Use Baseten | Use Aegis | Notes |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| Rapid prototyping / demos | ✅ | ⚪️ | Baseten: fastest path to public API. Aegis: more setup but repeatable. |
+| Sensitive / regulated data | ❌ | ✅ | Aegis supports on-prem, Keycloak, KMS, evidence capture, audit. |
+| Multi‑provider QPU jobs / Slurm orchestration | ❌ | ✅ | Baseten doesn't provide QPU/Slurm/HPC features. |
+| Device/OTA & edge fleets | ❌ | ✅ | Aegis includes fleet controllers, PKI and staged rollouts. |
+| Billing & chargeback per tenant | ❌ | ✅ | Aegis records BillingRecord + reconciliation. |
+| Managed scaling & low ops | ✅ | ⚪️ | Baseten handles infra; Aegis requires SRE but is flexible. |
+| Cost-sensitive workloads | ⚪️ | ✅ | Baseten may be expensive at scale; Aegis enables locality, spot instances, and chargeback. |
+| Governance & evidence bundles (legal) | ❌ | ✅ | Aegis has audit, cosign, Object Lock evidence workflows. |
+
+Integration patterns (recommended)
+1. Hybrid: Use Baseten for low-risk public inference and Aegis for regulated/internal workloads.
+   - Promotion flow: Aegis registry -> SME approval -> Export to Baseten (automated Tekton task) with evidence capture.
+2. Baseten as a downstream runtime:
+   - Keep canonical metadata, lineage and governance in Aegis, but export artifacts to Baseten for serving.
+   - Always record the Baseten deployment id and evidence URI back into Aegis.
+3. Fail-safe: Do not permit automatic, unmanaged pushes to Baseten for high-cost or regulated models. Enforce Gatekeeper policy and manual approvals.
+
+Security & compliance checklist for Baseten integration
+- Keep Baseten API keys in Secrets Manager / Vault and fetch via IRSA / ExternalSecrets.
+- Record SME approval and evidence before publishing to Baseten.
+- Capture and sign evidence bundle with cosign and store in Object‑Locked S3.
+- Maintain a mapping (Aegis model id <-> Baseten deployment id) in the model registry for traceability.
+```
